{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/200515-hunters-and-supernatural-development","id":200515,"title":"Hunters and Supernatural Development","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-17T16:50:47-07:00","id":200515,"title":"Hunters and Supernatural Development","content":"Suppose a hunter from a Conspiracy undergoes a transformation to templated supernatural creature (Awakens, perfects a blood bathing ritual, is taken by/escapes from a Keeper, etc.). Would they still retain access to the supernatural Endowments the conspiracy taught them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T23:00:42-07:00","id":200757,"title":"","content":"It depends on the template and the endowments in question, according to Spirit Slayers, which lists the main rulesbook endowments and states specific reasons as to why werewolves can't possess the specific endowments. Although for what it's worth, some of the assumptions they make are wrong according to the rules of WtF. <br /> <br /> When a hunter becomes a slasher for example, they keep their endowments, and while slasher isn't technically a template considering Masks can take a nuke to the face and only take one level of damage I don't think there is anyone who argues that all slashers are nonsupernatural.<br /> <br /> Compacts and Conspiracies makes mention of Cheiron giving supernatural snitches thaumatech implants, and Slashers mentions the possibility of Vanguard recruiting psychics ala Second Sight among their number, although how much that is worth considering GMC made many of the psychic powers available as supernatural merits is up in the air. <br /> <br /> So you have to think of how the template in question is different from a normal human, and how the endowments work, and figure out if there would be incompatibility problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T02:33:02-07:00","id":203668,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's best adjudicated on a case by case basis. Advanced Armory just represents your qualification and authorization to use and requisition that particular set of gear. If you're the US Government's Personal Vampire, they might let you keep the toys. But Elixirs depend on a human metabolism acclimated to alchemical mixtures, and being a vampire likely vitiates that entirely. Relic is already a merit anyone can take; unless the relic in question has a problem with being a vampire, it continues to work. The Goetic Gospels likely depend on the abyssal sympathy present within an unawakened soul; you lose access if you become a Mage. <br /> <br /> Case by case. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T03:40:20-07:00","id":203713,"title":"","content":"Advanced Armory requires an RFID chip to function in almost all cases, but if you can snag that and the tech itself, you should be good to go. Relics should work in anyone's hands. Thaumatechnology is tough; I'd say it works fine for witches (who are biologically human), is tough for werewolves, and never work for vampires (as they are dead, rendering a living implant pointless). Rites of Denial would work for anyone, so long as you had the ritual and some Cainite blood. All you need for Ink to work is the Angel to give it to you.<br /> <br /> Castigation requires demonic ancestry; if you don't have it, you're out of luck. The Ascending Ones do a vague <i>something</i> in order to make it so that their Elixirs don't kill them; to anyone without that training, they're just poison. Goetic Gospels require both training from the Knights of Saint George (and if you tie-in with Mage, the tie to the Abyss all Sleepers have) in order to work. Teleinformatics require the Wintergreen procedure, which only the VASCU has access to. I'm not sure about Rites du Cheval; I feel like anyone who wasn't a genuine Mystere would just end up regular, plain old possessed.<br /> <br /> I have no idea where to fall regarding Benedictions; maybe any truly faithful Catholic could make it happen? No fucking clue.<br /> <br /> Anthropophagy is weird and I don't know how the Faithful of Shulpae train recruits to do it. That said, a vampire that eats other monsters to gain their power? Fucking awesome.<br /> <br /> EDIT: ...and I totally missed what this thread was about, mixing it up for &quot;can supernaturals <i>gain</i> Endowments?&quot; Whoops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T21:45:07-07:00","id":204656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/200515-hunters-and-supernatural-development?p=203713#post203713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: ...and I totally missed what this thread was about, mixing it up for &quot;can supernaturals <i>gain</i> Endowments?&quot; Whoops.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, six of one...your ideas are still valid; you just approached the basic question from the other direction.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T23:13:06-07:00","id":204696,"title":"","content":"Lol, I imagine that's happened to the best of us, Atamajakki. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Actually, I meant to be more specific when I mentioned that Cheiron snitches get thaumatech, the examples given are witches and vampires, so obviously thaumatech does work for the undead. Which makes sense when you think about it, cheiron has no trouble grafting undead parts to living humans, why would living parts onto an undead patient stump them? <br /> <br /> As for castigation, it depends on morality, according to spirit slayers werewolves don't qualify because their morality meter changed in the transformation, so presumably any monster type that keeps morality/integrity could keep castigation, I'd also argue that monsters whose morality track is an addition to morality/integrity instead of a replacement should theoretically keep castigation too, but that's just my opinion. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}